it's been nearly a week since apple  announced ipad os 16 at wwdc which adds  a lot of much requested features to the  ipads and now after we've used it tried  it out seen its limitations does ipad os  16 fix the biggest issues with ipads and  specifically the ipad pros well let's  talk about that now ipads have been  crazy powerful for many years now but  the biggest limitation was the software  and that hit much harder when apple  added the m1 chip into the ipad pros the  hardware is mind blowing but the  software is very lacking almost  insultingly lacking that's why we put  out a review of the ipad pro saying that  apple really needs to step up and  everybody agreed and going as far as not  buying these because you don't really  get that much extra use out of the extra  power well what did apple add this year  what does it fix and what is still very  lacking so let's start out with the  simple things we have the weather app  now i don't know how many people really  care about this i typically use this on  my iphone but this is the best weather  app when you click on something you have  this full detailed view hour by hour you  have a lot of info about other quality  as far as like uv air quality this thing  is incredible and that's thanks to apple  buying out a company a couple years ago  that gives it this much data i don't  think this is a huge deal though for the  ipad one thing that i appreciate with my  terrible handwriting is a new  straightening feature so when you've  written some text it's all over the  place like this you could actually go  hold it down and then hit straighten now  as you see it doesn't fix my terrible  handwriting but it made it look a lot  better the next thing i really  appreciate is the display scaling option  so you can go over select displays  scroll all the way down and go to  display zoom and just hit more space now  since it's going to restart the ipad um  it doesn't really do that it seems like  it just turns the screen off and then  turns it back on so now everything got  smaller now as you can see we actually  can't add any more applications here we  just have more space between these  applications but then if you go into say  safari you'll actually get a little  refresh and all the text is smaller and  of course if you're using  things that you want to see a lot more  of you want to be more efficient have  more real estate this adds it now one of  my biggest complaints was the files app  with ipad os 15 apple made a couple  updates we finally had a transfer bar  that actually told us the speed which  was nice but it was still severely  lacking now we have this list view where  we have dates we have sizes available to  see we have this sub menu when you open  something up that gives you different  options we can actually go in and show  extensions on all these files so you  know what kind of file it is and then  when you rename it you can actually  change the extension as well now  obviously i shouldn't have done that for  a png but just to show you guys we have  a lot more power we also have  customizable toolbars a system wide undo  and a redesigned find and replace but  some of the things we really asked for  were not added to the files app for  example i just tried to plug in my  external hard drive to show you guys  something and i accidentally tugged on  it while it was being accessed and now  when i plug it in it just simply won't  show up and that's because it has a  little corruption from it being  unplugged accidentally this has happened  to me numerous times over the last year  and then i have to get out a mac or a pc  to be able to plug it in and use the  disk utility to run first aid and  quickly fix this issue and bam now we  can plug it in and our four terabyte ssd  shows up this is something that should  be available on the ipad pro when you're  spending this much money now along with  that the other thing that we needed was  the ability to format a hard drive not  all hard drives or ssds are compatible  and when they aren't you can't format  them to make them work like you can on  mac os or in windows or even on  eight-year-old android tablets so if you  want to erase your drive or you want to  reformat it or partition it you're still  going to need a mac and that should be  built into your files app with all the  crazy ai software stuff they've been  working on that's incredible they should  just be able to make this work it's not  a huge deal now with that we also have a  new reference mode under displays if you  have the 12.9 inch ipad like i do you  can go over here select reference mode  then it allows you to do some fine  tuning but it also allows you to plug  into a mac and then you can use this at  a display that will match specific  professional work cases which is nice  now they do actually have a reference  mode on apple's studio display which is  not a mini led display so i wonder why  it's only limited to the 12.9 inch model  and finally for probably the most  requested feature better less limiting  multitasking and external display  support when apple showed off stage  manager on stage i was super happy  until we got more news about the  limitations of it now let's go ahead and  start off show you how to use it this is  technically kind of like a separate app  it's kind of weird to do you open up  this little pull down the control center  you select that and we are in stage  manager now you don't see anything until  you start opening up some applications  and now we have this window here so  right here i have multiple different  tabs i can also go ahead and grab let's  say my apple music even though i don't  have it logged in here and i can switch  behind it so we finally have one app  open behind another one we can actually  go ahead and make this smaller you can  actually copy and paste from it and you  can pair apps together like this and  then let's say we go back to the files  app bam you swap through here you know  what i want files and i want my mail and  now i can actually just use four fingers  and switch through these applications i  can have different pairings and it does  work pretty well you can in fact make  one of these windows smaller so you have  two of them side by side and i can even  add another one here there you go we  have three applications opened side by  side and then let me go ahead and swipe  through go to my files app overall i am  very happy with this new edition and it  does work well and then if you're not a  fan of it just turn it off and you could  use your regular side-by-side  applications  the biggest issue is the fact that this  is m1 exclusive and it doesn't make  sense why there's a lot of proof that it  shouldn't be i'll explain in just a sec  now one thing that this does also add  finally is external display support  properly in the past with ipad os 15 you  can use mirror display but then you have  these giant black bars on the side  just like that you guys actually just  saw it there for a split second alright  guys so it looks like it is just bugged  out and no matter what i do it is stuck  with the old frustrating version of  having an external display support i  tried three displays restarted there's  no beta update so it's just stuck right  now but as apple showed off on stage it  does work when it's not buggy and it  works great you have a full external  display without those bars you can have  different applications there that you  can open up and run other apps on your  ipad at the same time this is what we've  wanted for years now so since stage  manager works so well why are so many  people upset well the first one there's  no pro apps the apple has been rumored  working on certain stuff we wish we can  get some better applications to make use  of the hardware that didn't happen but  the biggest one is the fact that stage  manager is limited to only m1 ipads and  it just doesn't make sense why that  would happen  now digitimes actually reached out to  apple and they asked why is this the  case and apple said that they are only  allowing it for m1s because it can use  memory swap and access more ram to run  these applications now on first stop  that kind of makes sense all right well  you have multiple apps open you can  switch through them it needs more ram  but if we dig a little bit deeper you  will see that the ipad air 4 with the  a14  actually supports this memory swap  function if you have a 256 gigabyte  version and with that if you have the  base m1 ipad with 64 gig that one does  not yet it does support the stage  manager and external display functions  now some people will say well the m1 has  eight gigs of ram already so maybe that  is why  but older ipads can actually run three  different sets of apps from multitasking  also with picture and picture included  and now with stage manager when we go up  here and we enable this little sidebar  we have four sets that are open so maybe  for the older ipads if it's a ram issue  the ipad pros the previous ones have six  gigs of ram why not just give us three  options instead of four those ipads can  already run that even worse ipads can  now along with that if we take another  step back i was thinking about it and  the a12z in the 2020 ipads that  processor was actually put into apple's  arm transition kit for apple silicon and  that was running full on mac os with  terminal with pro applications  with that processor from the ipad so if  that can run full-on mac os why can't we  run stage manager on at least the ipad  pros from  and  2018-2012  in reality once i did some more digging  there are different reputable people  that are agreeing with this and also one  that actually said that there is code  that will allow older ipads to run it  that you can flag and enable there's no  reason why memory swapping is needed for  simple resizing of application and  allowing an external display to be  connected without these bars here just  to send data over  that is just crazy tablets android  tablets from five six seven years ago  could do these kind of things without  any issues and everybody knows that ipad  os in ios is a lot more memory efficient  than android is i think we all know the  truth apple needs to sell more ipads  that was actually the only category that  declined by 14  compared to macs and iphones and  everything else that actually gained  sales  in the last quarterly reports so people  aren't buying these m1s because the  software just doesn't take advantage of  it and their older ipads do the job just  fine so how does apple get them to  update well they gave them a feature  that is exclusive to the m1s a feature  that works incredibly well gives you  more pro capabilities and you just have  to upgrade to get that now that is  really unfortunate i think we should be  able to have this on other ipads but  this is apple's choice this is what  they're pushing and people will upgrade  because of this  now of course there's other things that  are kind of missing for example the lock  screen functionality with ios the new  widgets that's very nice why can't we  have this on this large display when  you're in the lock screen i'm not sure  maybe they will end up adding that  but overall if you're an owner of an m1  ipad you're going to be very happy but  everybody else is very frustrated that  they are stuck in the past the same  thing goes to people have iphone sevens  with ios  16. technically it should be supported  even if they dropped the 6s last year  the 6s supported ios 15 and now apple is  dropping two years of devices to get  people to upgrade all the to all the  nice software improvements with ios 16.  so pete apple wants people to upgrade  that is very clear you guys let me know  your thoughts down in the comment  section below was this a good enough  upgrade to ipad os to make it more pro  and to make it worth it i want to hear  you guys thoughts click that circle  above to subscribe to see more videos  like this one check out one of those  great ones right over there this is mid  max and i'll see you in the next video  [Music]

